#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331511 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "141d61c7-1d82-52fe-b977-19daa910da9b" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring Alternative Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee2da2c1-5a07-5066-8fb1-676dc97c7b8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{tan}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331513} {:answer/id #uuid "8d309930-0175-5bed-a197-f9587dd91f42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡x+{tan}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331514} {:answer/id #uuid "23a12974-1118-5425-a03e-23cbbeb9268f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+{tan}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331515} {:answer/id #uuid "8f7fd32f-5376-5f12-a964-ca9d5947c94a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331516} {:answer/id #uuid "4898f65e-e62f-543f-9aa0-56039109f408" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d309930-0175-5bed-a197-f9587dd91f42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡x+{tan}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331514} :answer-field/id #uuid "64ac0b97-ae28-5c71-8175-8041b36aa265" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331512}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "816a7b5d-7d2b-59fc-bd5e-93ad35d7edfe" :question/math-academy-id "q-65399" :question/problem "Simplify ${sec}^{4}⁡x-{tan}^{4}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we can simplify our expression by factoring it as a difference of squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sec}^{4}⁡x-{tan}^{4}⁡x & =({sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x)({sec}^{2}⁡x+{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can rewrite our expression using $(3),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x)({sec}^{2}⁡x+{tan}^{2}⁡x) & =(1)({sec}^{2}⁡x+{tan}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡x+{tan}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{sec}^{4}⁡x-{tan}^{4}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x+{tan}^{2}⁡x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331518 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b14ef98-8122-512a-9cce-6e44392959d8" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring and Using Various Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ee9b21f-cd62-55b8-94bb-30f712f37f33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331520} {:answer/id #uuid "cfa89f69-f329-5f5b-b7c6-ba2401e3d161" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331521} {:answer/id #uuid "7b440d5b-af78-5eca-bfdf-78411ec00c16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331522} {:answer/id #uuid "4e7e38c9-fdf2-55c3-b031-edce6c165f4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331523} {:answer/id #uuid "6cf81a91-c1b9-58f4-815a-b95bb2ac3662" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b440d5b-af78-5eca-bfdf-78411ec00c16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331522} :answer-field/id #uuid "47aae9bf-585f-59cd-9e13-87baf7084e0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331519}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6a821d69-3cb9-5c4a-9785-e02e8036266b" :question/math-academy-id "q-65400" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${sec}^{2}⁡\\theta {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sec}^{4}⁡\\theta +2{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(3),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sec}^{4}⁡\\theta +2{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 & =-{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta ({sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta )+2{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & =-{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot (1)+2{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & =-{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta +2{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we can further simplify our expression using $(2)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta +2{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & ={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sec}^{4}⁡\\theta +2{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331525 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "141d61c7-1d82-52fe-b977-19daa910da9b" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring Alternative Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0d6a6b6-40ce-5551-868a-adf95cee771e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331527} {:answer/id #uuid "b621a88e-cfb6-5d36-955c-f3cdeae769a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331528} {:answer/id #uuid "a76baf1a-76e1-5091-9e37-6cb5e723ba01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡\\alpha " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331529} {:answer/id #uuid "a551f56b-bb35-59a4-a705-6600c14b8475" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡\\alpha +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331530} {:answer/id #uuid "3e9cd08f-e83e-59c5-9469-837f0c1cae29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e9cd08f-e83e-59c5-9469-837f0c1cae29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331531} :answer-field/id #uuid "5eaa2d93-7016-54cb-a39e-e6ad762be7bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331526}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2db73422-d97a-5f74-9a86-860248027e3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-65410" :question/problem "Simplify $\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha }{{tan}^{2}⁡\\alpha +\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha +1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\alpha ={sec}^{2}⁡\\alpha  \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡\\alpha ={sec}^{2}⁡\\alpha -1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡\\alpha -{tan}^{2}⁡\\alpha =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha }{{tan}^{2}⁡\\alpha +\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha +1} & =\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\alpha -1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha +1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\alpha +\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can further simplify our expression by factoring it out, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\alpha +\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha } & =\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha }{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha (\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha +1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha }}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha \\cancel{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha +1)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha }{{tan}^{2}⁡\\alpha +\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha +1}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331532 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b14ef98-8122-512a-9cce-6e44392959d8" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring and Using Various Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e403142-3d3f-5f6f-a42a-d72b52af3009" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331534} {:answer/id #uuid "35f395de-71e2-535f-8e80-21eea1177a5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{tan}^{4}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331535} {:answer/id #uuid "a9032168-7c1b-51a9-8962-3f60a94b5fbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x){tan}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331536} {:answer/id #uuid "f84ad0f3-8593-5b19-8b01-5f46789f0e4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x){tan}^{3}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331537} {:answer/id #uuid "8059ab97-895c-5341-a50a-e6979ca25a94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{tan}^{4}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331538}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9032168-7c1b-51a9-8962-3f60a94b5fbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x){tan}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331536} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b6b2448-6cce-5d43-9a34-d0e050735757" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331533}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3309aa28-d6ca-59c8-be57-306a349ee257" :question/math-academy-id "q-74157" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${sec}^{4}⁡x-{sec}^{2}⁡x?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sec}^{4}⁡x-{sec}^{2}⁡x & ={sec}^{2}⁡x\\cdot ({sec}^{2}⁡x-1) \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can use $(1),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sec}^{2}⁡x{tan}^{2}⁡x & =(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x){tan}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{sec}^{4}⁡x-{sec}^{2}⁡x=(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x){tan}^{2}⁡x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331539 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b14ef98-8122-512a-9cce-6e44392959d8" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring and Using Various Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36b0228b-bc89-564a-9f71-cbd89d964f65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331541} {:answer/id #uuid "c2b3a5e9-1298-55fa-b82b-da4ff292e724" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331542} {:answer/id #uuid "ab8e284e-0ccd-5de0-8851-d3c878cd4179" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{tan}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331543} {:answer/id #uuid "a73330cf-ea44-5644-8995-eb88f2b53ff9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331544} {:answer/id #uuid "b1d77d37-f139-59f6-b866-3b15ed2dd810" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1d77d37-f139-59f6-b866-3b15ed2dd810" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331545} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5dc9976-648d-5eef-9f2e-059ccceabc1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331540}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5cba60cb-dccb-5427-97e9-ae0742b85ca8" :question/math-academy-id "q-74162" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${sec}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor our expression, as follows:\n\n$$\n{sec}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x({sec}^{2}⁡x-1)\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡x({sec}^{2}⁡x-1)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the identity:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\n$$\n\nUsing the above identity, we can further simplify our expression, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{sec}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.\n$$"}]}
